  "solution": "**Given: **\n\n{ X} = 3 + 2sqrt 2 \n\n**Concept used:**\n\n(a-(1)/(a))² = a² + (1)/(a²) - 2\n\n**Calculation:**\n\n{ X} = 3 + 2√ 2 \n\n⇒ { (1)/(X)} = (1)/(3 + 2√ 2 )\n\n⇒ { (1)/(X)} = (3 -2√ 2 )/((3 + 2√ 2)(3 - 2√ 2 ) )\n\n⇒ { (1)/(X)} = (3 - 2√ 2 )/(3² - (2√ 2 )² )\n\n⇒ { (1)/(X)} = (3 - 2√ 2 )/(9 - 8)\n\n⇒ { (1)/(X)} = {3 - 2√ 2 }\n\nNow,\n\nLet √ { X} - (1)/({√ { X) }} be a\n\nSo, (√ { X} - (1)/({√ { X) }})² = a²\n\n⇒ √ { X}² + (1)/({√ { X²) }} -2 = a2\n\n⇒ X + (1)/({X) } -2 = a2\n\n⇒ 3 + 2√2 + 3 - 2√2 - 2 = a2\n\n⇒ 6 - 2 = a²\n\n⇒ 4 = a2\n\n⇒ a = 2 = sqrt { X} - (1)/({sqrt { X) }}\n\n**∴ The required answer is 2.**\n\n163:Tf0a,\n<p style=\"",
